cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. It contains text and code written with a large language model (Claude), with ideas and literature explored using OpenAI ChatGPT and DeepSeek, and results that are partly unverified (see the paper, section Limitations and provenance)."
title: "Pythagorean Specializations of an Elliptic K3 Surface: Geometry, Conductors, Root Numbers and Rank Jumps"
authors:
  - name: "Chalolennox"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-06
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Chalolennox/pythagorean-k3-specializations"
abstract: "Elliptic curves y^2 = x^3 + 4Ax - 8B from Pythagorean triples form an elliptic K3 surface. Working paper, code and data on their conductors, root numbers and rank jumps, and on the parity problem along the orbit t_n = 1 - x(nP). LLM-assisted; partly unverified."
keywords:
  - elliptic curves
  - K3 surfaces
  - root numbers
  - parity problem
